Z||000000||mrfixit58||06-07-2000||04:08 PM||||I just have to someone who cares... My bid for the Bubblegum Blue 1987 GT was a winner!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> Now it's time to start the long waiting game. I live in Florida and the car is in California. If everything goes OK I should see it in 2-3 weeks.<P>This is the car that I wanted someone to go look at for me. It was very short notice and the location was too remote but, I E-mailed the seller and he responded with all the right answers so... I bid on it and WON! That's when I came to my senses and started worrying about how to get it home  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>Once again, one of our ranks came to the rescue... DXR_DAD!! (Thanks DAD!) He called me and gave me the number to reach his brother who's in the moving business. I left a message and hope to hear from him today or tomorrow.<P>I'll post pictures when it arrives. Some of you may have already seen it... it was on eBay. Here are the stats: 87 GT, Bubblegum Blue (you know that already)in good shape, gray interior, 5-speed, one small tear in the driver's seat (have replacement already), cold A/C, cruse control needs work, new clutch a year ago, sunroof, PW, PB, PM. <P>I hope the real thing lives up to the pictures. We'll see soon!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Roy||||reg||1
